0214: precache enhanced lighting's own render targets

The pipeline cache records configs without the render target they are drawn into, and the
precache built every known config for the scene and offscreen layouts only. The variants enhanced
lighting derives for its passes (the depth pre-pass and the light shadow-map casters:
ShaderConfig::depthOnly / lightDepth, drawn into a depth-only target; the glow buffer: additive
draws without depth and alpha writes, drawn into the RGBA16F glow target) were therefore compiled
on first use in play: 100-600 ms frames (LM: docs/INTERPOLATION.md "Pass 5"). Such configs are now
also built for those layouts (the depth variants only for theirs).

